{
  "name": "Publish to social media from any app with a webhook and PostWire",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## A social publishing endpoint for any app\nFor developers and no-code builders who want one URL that publishes to every network — from a CRM, a form tool, Zapier, a script or a button. Send an idea and a list of networks; get back what was published where.\n\n### How it works\n1. **Webhook** receives a POST with JSON: { \"idea\": \"...\", \"networks\": [\"linkedin\",\"bluesky\"], \"id\": \"optional-unique-id\" }.\n2. **Valid request?** checks the idea and networks are there; if not, it answers 400 with what to send.\n3. **PostWire** writes a native post per network and publishes it. Send an id to make retries safe: the same id never posts twice.\n4. **Return the results** answers with one entry per network: ok, url, and a hint if it failed.\n\n### Setup\n1. Install the **PostWire** community node (Settings → Community nodes → `n8n-nodes-postwire`), then create a free account at postwire.io, connect your networks and paste the API key into a **PostWire API** credential.\n2. Add a Header Auth credential to the Webhook so only your apps can call it.\n3. Activate the workflow and call the production URL.\n\n### Customize\nAccept media_url in the body and set Media to URL, or switch to Schedule and accept a date.\n\n*Uses a community node, so it runs on self-hosted n8n.*",
        "height": 672,
        "width": 520
      },
      "id": "4e3fed51-05ee-491e-aa23-bf3154ef165b",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -647,
        -217
      ]
    },
